    # ☽'Sanctteinvaus — Private Ledger (second binding)
    
    ---
    
    **7th dim, mid-season**
    
    Shipment from L-4 shaft: 14 cores, grade oss-mid, warmth-radius acceptable. Two cracked in transit — Taemov~ blames the new carts but he's been careless since his clutch-mate moved to cold-quarters. I said nothing. Tunnel-drip pitch higher today near the east fork, which means pressure shift, which means check the seals tomorrow. Left flipper aching. Ate half a ration of rendered fat and couldn't finish. The brazier in my alcove is dimming faster than it should. Replaced it. Fine now.
    
    ---
    
    **9th dim**
    
    The hum stopped.
    
    I felt it go — not heard, *felt*, the way you feel a bone-clasp loosen before it falls. Was mid-count on the aurora-crystal inventory (24 units, grade — no. I can't do notation right now.) Went down to the root-junction with ☽'irtoius and the vein was — it was open. Wide. Cold breathing out of it like a mouth. The miners standing there not speaking. Not speaking because what do you say when
    
    [struck through: We built this. I surveyed that fissure myself, twenty-three seasons ago, my left flipper still worked and I]
    
    The arithmetic. Already doing the arithmetic. 14 cores in stock. Colony draw per dim-cycle is 6. Forges need 3 minimum or the tool-lines stop. The Stack shipment is due and they'll want their 8 and I don't — I can't —
    
    Someone was whispering behind me in the junction. ☽'irtouis said no one was there. Tunnel acoustics. Obviously tunnel acoustics.
    
    The vein was still warm when I checked. Just barely.
    
    ---
    
    **12th dim**
    
    Three days and the temperature in my warren has dropped enough that the meltwater on the west wall refroze. I'm logging this because I need to *see* the numbers or I'll lose my mind: 6 cores remaining. Colony draw reduced to 4 per cycle, which means the deep warrens are going dark. Rationing started yesterday. Plunge-caller ☽'Setilmelum'Tier wants to seal off the lower levels entirely and I told him if we do that we lose the shadow-labs and every tool cached below junction six. He looked at me like I was haggling over inventory while the world freezes. Maybe I am.
    
    The Stack sent a courier. Measured words. Consensus-approved sympathy. *Stellar parallax* of the situation. They want to know about the next shipment. Of course they do. They need us and they hate needing us and they wrap it in aurora-light and celestial metaphor and I — I need them too. The Accord is a contract with nothing behind it now and they know and I know and we'll both pretend otherwise because what else is there.
    
    I keep thinking about the Veil☽ Glow materials I sourced for the shadow-labs, seasons back. Fire hidden inside aurora-ice. The invisible burn. My flippers ache when I think about it and I don't know why and I'm not writing down why.
    
    They found Kelm by the sealed passage. Two cores in her flippers. I owed her three units of aurora-crystal and now that debt goes — where? Where does it go?
    
    Something in the ice remembers the price.
    
    I did not write that last line.
    
    ---
    
    **19th dim**
    
    Sealed the root-fissure with bone-ash. ☽'irtouis led the prayer-silence, which I attended and will not discuss. Temperature holding. Barely. Orca raids topside mean the north exits stay blocked so we're running escorts through the deep lateral — armed, when arms are available. Stack sent 12 aurora-crystals, unsolicited. I inventoried them without looking directly. Hands steady. Flipper steady. New carts arriving from Taemov~. Life continues. Debt continues.
    
    ---
    
    **21st dim**
    
    Drip-pitch wrong again. Brazier dims. Something patient in the east fork.
    
    Need candles.
  CANONICAL_CHRONICLE
  annotation "note_1771588340877_0", anchor: "Something patient in the east fork", text: "She names it three times without naming it. The junction whisper ☽'irtouis couldn't source. The line she disavows writing. And now — *patient*. Not hostile. Patient. The deep ice holds impressions from before any penguin civilization existed. When fissures open and old seals break, what breathes out is not always geothermal. The Nightshelf claim the watchers are real. ☽'Sanctteinvaus, Nightshelf to her marrow, claims nothing — just keeps recording what she notices. That restraint frightens me more than naming them would.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771588340877_1", anchor: "They found Kelm by the sealed passage", text: "Found. Not rescued. Carrying warmth toward a door that doesn't open. The Walking seizes those who have lost much — but it takes them *outward*, onto the ice. Kelm went deeper. I note only that she carried a debt ☽'Sanctteinvaus could not repay, and that the compulsion does not always announce itself by direction.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771588340877_2", anchor: "I did not write that last line", text: "I believe her. The lower archive holds documents where ice-memory bleeds through — sentences in no one's hand, thermal signatures from the wrong century, marginalia the author never wrote. My left flipper knows what proximity to that kind of intrusion costs. She was sharp enough to notice and honest enough to flag it. Most aren't. The line the ice contributed — *Something in the ice remembers the price* — is, of course, true. That's the worst part.", type: :tangent, display: :full
